Stem export test (Audio > Export Stems...)
==========================================

Runs MusE headless (Qt offscreen platform, dummy audio driver) on a generated
project, exports stems through the real dialog and checks the files sample by
sample. Needs g++, pkg-config with Qt5Widgets and python3 (standard library only).

  tests/stem_export/run.sh [path/to/muse]          # default: build/muse/muse4
  STEMTEST_FREEWHEEL=0 tests/stem_export/run.sh    # render in real time

  # Also midi tracks sharing one synth (the bundled synths must be installed):
  make -C build install DESTDIR=/tmp/museinst
  STEMTEST_APPDIR=/tmp/museinst tests/stem_export/run.sh

The project (make_song.py) has two stereo wave tracks of noise, "A" and "B",
and an aux track that "A" sends to at 0.5. It is exported once with the range
markers and once with the markers "Intro" and "Verse". check_stems.py then
requires for every stem:

  - exactly the number of frames of its range or section,
  - starting exactly at the first frame of it (it reports a shift if not),
  - A = a.wav * 1.5 (the track plus its aux return), B = b.wav (nothing of A).

It is also exported "through the output track's effects": all tracks go to the
output, whose fader is at 0.5, so then A = a.wav * 0.75 and B = b.wav * 0.5.

The midi project (miditest.med) has the midi tracks "M1" and "M2" playing the
same synth (vam) at different times. The stem of M1 must be silent where only M2
plays and the other way round, the stem of the synth track has both.

autotest_preload.cpp is loaded with LD_PRELOAD and drives the GUI; MusE runs
with HOME and the XDG folders set to the work folder, so the user's own
configuration is not used or changed.
